hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3041","\nNarrated to us Bundār, narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar, narrated to us Shuʿbah, on the authority of Abū Bishr, who said: I heard Saʿīd ibn Jubayr narrating from Ibn ʿAbbās (RA) that a woman vowed to perform Hajj, then she died before fulfilling it. Her brother came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and asked him about it. He said: “If your sister had a debt, would you pay it?” He said: “Yes.” He (ﷺ) said: “Then fulfill the right of Allāh, for He has more right to be fulfilled.”\n\nAnother chain from ʿAlī ibn Khashram, who informed us ʿĪsā, from Shuʿbah, from Jaʿfar ibn Iyās (Abū Bishr), with the same chain."
